' Observed behavior: Java discovery captures metadata; pi expands Skill body into model input.
' Target-only architecture: preserve original public input and a private recoverable expansion.
' Design reason: reuse one message admission and event projection; do not reinterpret new Skill versions on recovery.
skinparam shadowing false
actor Caller
participant "Command Application" as C
participant "Skill Execution Service" as S
participant "Immutable Invocation Snapshot" as I
participant "Shared Message Application" as A
database "Session / Context Store" as D
participant "Runtime / Event Projector" as R
participant "Event Query Application" as Q
Caller -> C : POST command: skill:name / arguments / files
C -> S : selected real Skill Definition
S -> I : resolve complete Agent / body / binding version
S -> S : validate expansion budget and trust boundary
S -> A : original user input + internal expansion snapshot
group Owning admission transaction
  A -> D : recheck access / binding / idle / capacity
  A -> D : append original public user event + private context\nregister root event and set running
  D --> A : committed receipt and fixed execution
end
A --> Caller : SSE: complete original user.message first
A -> R : execute with in-memory credentials
R -> D : ordered complete events / safe projection
R --> Caller : same root sourceEventId; preview best-effort
R -> D : confirming boundary or actual terminal
R --> Caller : matching idle; close response
Caller -> Q : GET Events for reconciliation
Q -> D : current visible complete history
D --> Caller : original invocation / output; no private Skill body
note over I,D
Freeze parsed body and metadata for this invocation.
Recheck mutable bindings under owning locks before acceptance.
Keep recoverable expansion in existing private Session context.
No separate Skill full-text audit copy; use deployment retention.
No raw credential persistence or automatic side-effect replay.
end note
@enduml
